<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 64,689 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 64,689 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 64,689 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 58,684 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    Feb 12</p>
<p>    Export cargo		18,963	21,841</p>
<p>    Import cargo		45,726	36,843</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, nine are expected to sail and seven are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Petroleum products    8,970	 Bakri Orbitor     14/2</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     16,000	 Elite		 15/2</p>
<p>Containers		  500	 Fen He		22/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
